      body: `# Resume & Career Kit

## 1 \u2014 Resume (ATS-safe, impact-first)
**Order**: contact \u2192 title line (the role you're targeting) \u2192 summary (2-3 lines, NOT an autobiography) \u2192 experience (reverse-chronological) \u2192 education \u2192 skills/projects (junior: projects/education higher).
**Every bullet = action + scope + result**: "\u0645\u0647\u0627\u062C\u0631\u062A \u067E\u0627\u06CC\u06AF\u0627\u0647\u200C\u062F\u0627\u062F\u0647 \u06F4\u06F0 \u062C\u062F\u0648\u0644\u06CC \u0628\u0647 PostgreSQL \u0628\u0627 \u06A9\u0627\u0647\u0634 \u0632\u0645\u0627\u0646 \u067E\u0627\u0633\u062E \u06F6\u06F2\u066A" \u2014 verbs first (built/led/migrated/automated/reduced), numbers ALWAYS (%, count, time, money \u2014 estimates honestly labeled "\u062D\u062F\u0648\u062F"). Weak bullets ("\u0645\u0633\u0626\u0648\u0644 \u0646\u06AF\u0647\u062F\u0627\u0631\u06CC \u0633\u0631\u0648\u0631\u0647\u0627 \u0628\u0648\u062F\u0645") tell the reader nothing; if you genuinely lack numbers, state scale (users, traffic, team size).
**ATS rules**: single-column, no tables/graphics/photos (unless the market expects them \u2014 Persian market often does for design roles; then keep a text version too), standard section names, .pdf, keywords from the actual job post woven into bullets (they have to be TRUE, mind), file name \`Name-Role.pdf\`.
**Length**: 1 page < 8 years experience; 2 pages max senior. Persian resume: \u0645\u0639\u06CC\u0627\u0631 register, Latin tech terms stay Latin, \u0646\u06CC\u0645\u200C\u0641\u0627\u0635\u0644\u0647 correct (recruiters notice).
**Cut**: "\u0639\u0644\u0627\u0642\u0647\u200C\u0645\u0646\u062F \u0628\u0647 \u062A\u06A9\u0646\u0648\u0644\u0648\u0698\u06CC", obvious skills listed as achievements, GPA below ~16 unless early-career, "references available" \u2014 everyone knows.

## 2 \u2014 Tailoring (the 15 minutes that triple replies)
Read the job post; find the top 5 requirements; make sure your top 5 bullets answer THEM (reorder/rewrite \u2014 same truth, aimed framing). Title line = their title (if honest). This beats applying to 3\xD7 more jobs untailored.

## 3 \u2014 Cover letter (short, human, specific)
Three paragraphs, half a page: (1) the hook \u2014 why THIS company specifically (something real: their product, a post, their stack) + the role; (2) the 2-3 most relevant proofs, with numbers; (3) the close \u2014 availability + one confident sentence. No "\u0628\u062F\u0648\u0646 \u0647\u06CC\u0686 \u062A\u062C\u0631\u0628\u0647\u200C\u0627\u06CC \u0627\u0645\u0627 \u062E\u06CC\u0644\u06CC \u0645\u0634\u062A\u0627\u0642\u0645". Persian market: \xAB\u0628\u0627 \u0633\u0644\u0627\u0645 \u0648 \u0627\u062D\u062A\u0631\u0627\u0645\xBB frame, then immediately concrete. Same truth rules: never invent.

## 4 \u2014 LinkedIn
Headline = value proposition (role + specialty + impact), not just current title. About = the 3-paragraph letter minus the ask + a closing CTA. Skills pinned to the target role; endorsements real; a handful of genuine project posts beat a silent profile.

## 5 \u2014 Interview prep
- **STAR bank**: prepare 6-8 stories (S-ituation, T-ask, A-ction, R-esult \u2014 R with numbers) covering: hardest bug, conflict, failure (OWNED), deadline save, leadership, something you built. Every behavioral question is a permutation of these six. Practice saying them in 90 seconds.
- Technical: fundamentals refreshed (they test the base of your claimed stack), YOUR PROJECTS cold (every line you claim, you defend), and honest "I don't know but I'd find out by\u2026" beats bluffing 10/10 times.
- Questions YOU ask (real ones): how is success measured at 6 months? what does the team lack that I'd fill? recent technical decision they regret/rejoice?
- Salary: deflect early ("\u062F\u0645 \u062F\u0633\u062A\u0645 \u0631\u0627 \u0645\u06CC\u200C\u0622\u0648\u0631\u0645\u061B \u0627\u0648\u0644 \u0645\u06CC\u200C\u062E\u0648\u0627\u0647\u0645 \u0645\u0637\u0645\u0626\u0646 \u0634\u0648\u0645 fit \u062F\u0631\u0633\u062A \u0627\u0633\u062A"), research market range first, then give a RANGE you'd accept the bottom of; negotiate the package (remote, review date, learning budget), not just base.

## 6 \u2014 Gaps & switches (handle proactively)
Career gap: one confident line in the summary/interview ("\u06F2 \u0633\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u0631\u0627\u0642\u0628\u062A \u0627\u0632 \u062E\u0627\u0646\u0648\u0627\u062F\u0647 \u2014 \u0628\u0627\u0632\u06AF\u0634\u062A\u0645 \u0648 \u0645\u062F\u0627\u0631\u06A9 X \u0631\u0627 \u06AF\u0631\u0641\u062A\u0645"), no apologizing. Field switch: lead with transferable PROOF (projects, certs, freelance) not with the story of why you left; the reader buys evidence, not motivation.`
